<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept soybean imports fall 10.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept soybean imports fall 10.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in September totalled 310,443 tonnes, down 10.6 percent from 347,316 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Sept 96	  Aug 96     Sept 95</p>
<p> Total imports    310,443	 307,617     347,316</p>
<p> Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		 192,918	 256,388     300,828</p>
<p> Brazil		32,226	  43,023	28,379</p>
<p> Paraguay	    74,788	   6,000	15,726</p>
<p> China		  5,043	     521	    92</p>
<p>Imports in the first nine months of 1996 totalled 3,611,248 tonnes, down one percent against 3,648,277 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3-3432-7431)</p>
</text>
